### Quick API checks (VS Code "REST Client" extension or Visual Studio). Start the API first.
@host = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Trainer login -> copy the token into @trainerToken below
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anita@example.com", "password": "Password@123", "role": "Trainer" }

### 2. Same user, wrong role -> must be 401 "Invalid email or password."
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anita@example.com", "password": "Password@123", "role": "Trainee" }

### 3. Trainee login -> copy the token into @traineeToken below
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "priya@example.com", "password": "Password@123", "role": "Trainee" }

###
@trainerToken = PASTE_TRAINER_TOKEN
@traineeToken = PASTE_TRAINEE_TOKEN

### 4. Trainer: list trainees
GET {{host}}/api/trainees
Authorization: Bearer {{trainerToken}}

### 5. Trainer: add trainee (run twice -> second time 409 on email, also try UPPER CASE email)
POST {{host}}/api/trainees
Authorization: Bearer {{trainerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test Intern", "email": "test.intern@example.com", "initialPassword": "Welcome@123" }

### 6. Trainer: create assignment
POST {{host}}/api/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{trainerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "traineeId": 2, "topic": "TypeScript Basics", "videoUrl": "https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/", "notes": "Read the handbook intro", "dueDate": "2026-12-10" }

### 7. Trainer: list assignments + summary
GET {{host}}/api/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{trainerToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{trainerToken}}

### 8. Trainee: my assignments + summary (Priya: total 5, completed 2, overdue 1, 40%)
GET {{host}}/api/assignments/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{traineeToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{traineeToken}}

### 9. Trainee: read own assignment (id 5 = React Basics) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/assignments/5
Authorization: Bearer {{traineeToken}}

### 10. Trainee: read ANOTHER trainee's assignment (id 6 belongs to Rahul) -> must be 404
GET {{host}}/api/assignments/6
Authorization: Bearer {{traineeToken}}

### 11. Trainee: update status
PATCH {{host}}/api/assignments/5/status
Authorization: Bearer {{traineeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Completed" }

### 12. Trainee tries a trainer endpoint -> must be 403
GET {{host}}/api/trainees
Authorization: Bearer {{traineeToken}}

### 13. No token -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/assignments/mine
